1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,469
You Got My Name Almost Right.

3
00:00:03,469 --> 00:00:06,354
Emma and I order sandwiches at a busy cafe.

4
00:00:06,354 --> 00:00:11,865
The person at the register asks for my name, but the coffee machine starts making a loud noise just as I answer.

5
00:00:12,148 --> 00:00:14,035
Sorry, what was that?

6
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:15,480
Lucy.

7
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:16,829
Got it.

8
00:00:16,829 --> 00:00:18,454
Two sandwiches.

9
00:00:18,454 --> 00:00:20,319
We'll call you when they're ready.

10
00:00:20,596 --> 00:00:22,965
We find a table near the pickup counter.

11
00:00:22,965 --> 00:00:26,704
Emma takes off her jacket, and I watch people walk past the window.

12
00:00:26,704 --> 00:00:30,215
A minute later, someone calls out a name I don't recognize.

13
00:00:30,484 --> 00:00:31,634
Lucky!

14
00:00:31,634 --> 00:00:33,176
Order for Lucky!

15
00:00:33,410 --> 00:00:34,579
Are we lucky today?

16
00:00:34,579 --> 00:00:36,797
Because those look a lot like our sandwiches.

17
00:00:37,084 --> 00:00:39,171
I walk over and check the bag.

18
00:00:39,171 --> 00:00:42,276
One cheese sandwich, one turkey sandwich.

19
00:00:42,276 --> 00:00:44,005
I think that's my order.

20
00:00:44,284 --> 00:00:45,442
Lucky?

21
00:00:45,676 --> 00:00:47,493
Lucy, actually.

22
00:00:47,493 --> 00:00:48,961
Close enough.

23
00:00:49,228 --> 00:00:51,211
Oh, sorry about that.

24
00:00:51,211 --> 00:00:52,888
Could you spell that for me?

25
00:00:53,164 --> 00:00:55,751
L, U, C, Y.

26
00:00:55,751 --> 00:00:58,897
The clerk corrects the name on the receipt and gives me the bag.

27
00:00:58,897 --> 00:01:01,345
I thank her and bring lunch to our table.

28
00:01:01,562 --> 00:01:03,470
Congratulations on your new name.

29
00:01:03,470 --> 00:01:05,199
Does it come with extra cookies?

30
00:01:05,476 --> 00:01:06,970
Apparently not.

31
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:09,261
I check the bag just in case.

32
00:01:09,261 --> 00:01:11,522
Only sandwiches and napkins.

33
00:01:11,522 --> 00:01:15,928
But my sandwich has an especially big slice of cheese, so maybe I am lucky.

34
00:01:16,154 --> 00:01:18,364
Next time, I'll order under my name.

35
00:01:18,652 --> 00:01:19,927
Good idea.

36
00:01:19,927 --> 00:01:23,135
Let's see if you become Emily, Emma, or Excellent.

37
00:01:23,135 --> 00:01:25,969
I think Excellent would suit you for at least one lunch.
